# Configuration file for the SANE ix1300 backend.
# The backend controls a ScanSnap iX1300 on a Wi-Fi network.
# For more data, read the sane-ix1300(5) manual page.
#
# Lines that start with "#" are comments.
#
# The scanner feeds the whole stack in one job. Load only the sheets that
# you want to scan. The frontend sets the page limit (scanimage
# --batch-count). A cancel feeds out the rest of the stack without a
# scan; the SANE option --halt-on-cancel stops the paper in the paper
# path instead. This file has no setting for these functions.

# Scanner addresses.
# "net auto" sends a UDP broadcast and finds all iX1300 scanners.
# "net <ip>" sends a probe to one scanner. You can write more than one line.
net auto
#net 192.0.2.212

# Host ID (16 hex digits). The scanner keeps one registered host ID.
# The scanner refuses a host with a different ID (reserve result -6).
#hostid 0123456789ABCDEF

# Network interface. If you do not set it, the backend uses the route
# to the scanner.
#iface wlan0

# The longest time (in seconds) for one complete reply.
#timeout 30

# The scanner frees the reserve when it gets no keepalive packet for
# this time plus 10 seconds.
#reserve-timeout 30

# Time (in seconds) between two keepalive packets. It must be at most
# reserve-timeout + 5. The backend makes a longer value smaller.
#keepalive 15

# Time (in milliseconds) that the backend waits for discovery replies.
#discovery-timeout 3000

# UDP port for scan button packets. 0 lets the system select a port.
#trigger-port 0
